IMPORT prelude

-- Betting Control Act 1954 (Western Australia) -- whether a bet made in WA is lawful, with whom (the TAB, the wagering
-- licensee, a bookmaker licensed under the Act, an operator licensed elsewhere in Australia, an offshore operator, an
-- unlicensed bookmaker, a friend), the offences that fall on the person who bets rather than on the operator, children,
-- the court order that bookmakers and the TAB stop betting with a person (s 25), and disputes with a racecourse bookmaker.
--
-- SEAT: the gambler -- the individual in WA who bets on races and other events, and the child who wants to. Every decision
-- is phrased as the gambler would ask it: "What does the Act make of my bet", "What is the most I can be fined for this
-- bet", "Can a court order bookmakers not to bet with me".
--
-- Provisions covered: s 4(1) (bookmaker, to bet, fixed odds bet, offshore betting operator), s 4AA (betting exchange, as a
-- gloss), s 5(1), s 10J(2), s 12(3), (3b) (as one fact), s 21(1)(a), (b), (2)(b)-(d), (3)(a), (b), s 22(1), (2), s 22A,
-- s 23(1), (2), s 24(1)(b), (c), s 25(1)-(3), (5), s 26, s 26A(3), s 26B, s 26C(5), s 27A(1)-(3), s 28(2), s 30(1),
-- s 32(1)-(3).
--
-- Edition: the compilation incorporating amendments to the Gambling Legislation Amendment Act 2024 (No. 53 of 2024), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48877.txt (retrieved 7 September 2026). The deposit's uncommenced
-- provisions table lists most of the TAB (Disposal) Act 2019 (No. 21 of 2019) as "To be proclaimed"; Part 1A (wagering
-- licences, inserted by s 47 of that Act) is in force, and s 23 still names RWWA. No regulations are deposited: the Betting
-- Control Regulations (telephone and internet betting under s 12(3b)), the prescribed prohibited events, and the Gaming and
-- Wagering Commission Act 1987 (social gambling, permitted gaming) are asked as facts.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the licensing of bookmakers and the wagering licensee (Parts 1A and 2 except as glosses), levies and
-- totalisator finance (Part 3), race fields (ss 27D-27F), the duties of bookmakers, RWWA staff, racing clubs and licensed
-- premises (ss 21(1)(e), (3)(c)-(e), 25(3) as a gloss only, 26C(1), 27, 28C-28G, 29, 31), search and forfeiture of betting
-- material (ss 28(1), 28A, 28B), evidence (s 31A), discipline (s 32A). Machinery out: the Commission, delegation,
-- regulations, Part 6 transitional provisions. Lotto (Lotteries Commission Act 1990) and the casino (Casino Control Act
-- 1984) are other Acts.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Betting Control Act 1954 -- the gambler's questions`

§§ `who I bet with`

-- s 4(1): a "bookmaker" is a person who carries on the business of, or acts as, a bookmaker "and who holds a current
-- bookmaker's licence"; a "licence" is "a licence issued under this Act". A bookmaker licensed only in another State is
-- therefore not a "bookmaker" in this Act.
-- s 6(1): a "wagering licence may be granted ... to conduct totalisator betting and fixed odds betting on a race, event or
-- simulated race." Whether one has been granted is not in the deposit; it is asked by choosing this operator.
-- s 27A(1): an "offshore betting operator" (s 4(1)) is authorised by a law outside Australia; one "granted an exemption by
-- the Commission under this section" is an "authorised person".
-- s 4AA: a "betting exchange" lets persons bet with other persons through its operator. The Act names it only for race
-- fields and the racing bets levy (ss 14A, 27D); for the gambler it is an operator licensed somewhere or not.
DECLARE `Who I bet with` IS ONE OF
    `the TAB run by RWWA`                                   -- Racing and Wagering Western Australia: totalisator and fixed odds
    `the wagering licensee`                                 -- the holder of a wagering licence under s 6(1), if one is granted
    `a bookmaker licensed under this Act`                   -- s 4(1) "bookmaker"
    `an operator licensed in another State or Territory`    -- s 27A(1)(b); a betting exchange licensed there is one of these
    `an offshore operator the Commission has exempted`      -- s 27A(1)(c)
    `an offshore operator the Commission has not exempted`  -- s 4(1) "offshore betting operator", no s 27A(4) exemption
    `an unlicensed bookmaker`                               -- s 24(1)(b): carries on business as a bookmaker without a licence
    `a friend or workmate, privately`

DECLARE `My bet` HAS
    `who I bet with`                         IS A `Who I bet with`
    `my age in years`                        IS A NUMBER
    `I am in WA when I make it`              IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 23(1)(a) "a place in this State"; s 24(1) "any place in this State"
    `I make it by telephone or online`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 27A(1) "by telephone or electronically by means of the internet ..."
    `it is a fixed odds bet`                 IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 4(1): the amount to be won is fixed before the bet is accepted
    `the event is outside WA`                IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 27A(1)(a)
    `the Commission has approved bookmaking on the event under s 4B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `betting on the event is permitted by the law of another State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the event is a prescribed prohibited event or contingency` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 4(1); prescribed, so asked
    `I know, or would be expected to know, the operator is not authorised` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 27A(2), (3)(b)
    `the bookmaker takes it as the Act allows` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- s 12(3), (3b): in the betting area of a racecourse on a race day or approved day, or by telephone or internet
        -- betting "in accordance with the regulations" (not deposited, so asked as one fact)
    `it is social gambling or permitted gaming under the Gaming and Wagering Commission Act 1987` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 23(1)(e); borrowed

§§ `s 27A -- interstate and offshore bets`

-- s 27A(1): "interstate or offshore bet means a bet made -- (a) on an event or contingency outside the State; and (b) by
-- telephone or electronically by means of the internet, subscription television or any other online communications
-- system; and (c) with a person who is outside the State (including a person who is outside Australia)".
-- The operators in limb (c) are taken to be those licensed outside WA (the encoder's reading of who is "outside the State").
GIVEN `b` IS A `My bet`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator is outside WA` IF
    CONSIDER `b`'s `who I bet with`
    WHEN `an operator licensed in another State or Territory` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an offshore operator the Commission has exempted` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an offshore operator the Commission has not exempted` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Is my bet an interstate or offshore bet (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 27A(1))?
GIVEN `b` IS A `My bet` @desc Who you bet with, where the event is, and how you bet
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my bet an interstate or offshore bet` IF
        `b`'s `the event is outside WA`
    AND `b`'s `I make it by telephone or online`
    AND `the operator is outside WA` `b`

-- s 27A(1): "authorised person means -- (a) a bookmaker; or (b) a person authorised under the law of another State or
-- Territory to engage in or conduct betting on events; or (c) an offshore betting operator granted an exemption".
@export Is the operator I bet with an authorised person (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 27A(1))?
GIVEN `b` IS A `My bet` @desc Who you bet with
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the operator an authorised person` IF
    CONSIDER `b`'s `who I bet with`
    WHEN `a bookmaker licensed under this Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an operator licensed in another State or Territory` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an offshore operator the Commission has exempted` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 27A(1): "permitted event or contingency means -- (a) an event or contingency approved under section 4B(2); or (b) an
-- event or contingency, except a prohibited event or contingency, on which betting is permitted by the laws of another
-- State or a Territory."
@export Is the event a permitted event or contingency (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 27A(1))?
GIVEN `b` IS A `My bet` @desc Whether the event is approved, permitted elsewhere in Australia, or prohibited
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a permitted event` IF
        `b`'s `the Commission has approved bookmaking on the event under s 4B`
    OR (    `b`'s `betting on the event is permitted by the law of another State or Territory`
        AND (NOT `b`'s `the event is a prescribed prohibited event or contingency`))

-- s 27A(2): "A person in this State who makes an offshore bet with a person who the person making the bet knows, or would
-- be reasonably expected to know, is not an authorised person commits an offence." "Offshore bet" is not defined; the
-- encoding reads it as the defined "interstate or offshore bet".
-- (2A): "A person in this State who makes an interstate or offshore bet on an event or contingency that is not a
-- permitted event or contingency commits an offence." Penalty for each: a fine of $10 000.
@export Do I commit an offence under s 27A by making this bet (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 27A(2), (2A))?
GIVEN `b` IS A `My bet` @desc Who you bet with, the event, and what you knew
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence under s 27A` IF
        `b`'s `I am in WA when I make it`
    AND `Is my bet an interstate or offshore bet` `b`
    AND (   (    (NOT `Is the operator an authorised person` `b`)
             AND `b`'s `I know, or would be expected to know, the operator is not authorised`)
         OR (NOT `Is it a permitted event` `b`))

§§ `ss 5, 22, 23, 24, 27A -- what the Act makes of my bet`

-- s 23(1): "A person shall not personally or by means of an agent, or by post, telephone or other electronic means of
-- communication -- (a) make a bet at or in a place in this State ... unless -- (c) the place is [premises authorised under
-- s 5(2), a racecourse during a licensed meeting, the bookmakers' part of a racecourse, a registered place]; or (d) the bet
-- is made -- (i) by means of a totalisator authorised to operate under a written law; or (ii) as a fixed odds bet with RWWA
-- in accordance with a written law; or (iii) with a bookmaker in accordance with this Act; or (e) the bet constitutes
-- permitted gaming, or social gambling ..." Penalty: a fine of $100 000.
-- s 24(1): a person who "(b) bets with any other person who carries on, or purports to carry on, the business or vocation
-- of, or who acts as, a bookmaker but is not the holder of a current bookmaker's licence; or (c) bets with a bookmaker,
-- otherwise than in accordance with this Act ... at any time or at any place in this State, commits an offence." Penalty:
-- a fine of $100 000.
-- s 22(1): no person under 18 shall "(a) bet with a totalisator ... to which section 17B applies; or (b) bet with a
-- bookmaker ... licensed under this Act"; (2)(b): nor "make a bet with or through RWWA". Penalty: a fine of $2 000.
--
-- Read literally, ss 23(1) and 24(1)(b) reach a bet from WA with an operator licensed only in another State or offshore, and
-- s 23(1)(d) does not name a fixed odds bet with a wagering licensee. Yet s 27A sets out when an interstate or offshore bet
-- is an offence (implying the others are not), and Part 1A licenses fixed odds betting. Which reading a court takes is not
-- for the encoding to guess: those bets come out as `uncertain`.
DECLARE `What the Act makes of my bet` IS ONE OF
    `outside the Act: I am not in WA`
    `lawful: the Act allows it`
    `an offence by me`
    `uncertain: ss 23(1) or 24(1)(b) read literally reach it, though the Act licenses or tolerates it elsewhere`

`the age of majority` MEANS 18

@export What does the Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) make of my bet (ss 22, 23, 24, 27A)?
GIVEN `b` IS A `My bet` @desc Who you bet with, your age, where you are, the event, and how you bet
GIVETH A `What the Act makes of my bet`
DECIDE `What does the Act make of my bet` IS
    IF (NOT `b`'s `I am in WA when I make it`)
    THEN `outside the Act: I am not in WA`
    ELSE CONSIDER `b`'s `who I bet with`
         WHEN `the TAB run by RWWA` THEN
             IF `b`'s `my age in years` LESS THAN `the age of majority`
             THEN `an offence by me`                                          -- s 22(2)(b)
             ELSE `lawful: the Act allows it`                                 -- s 23(1)(d)(i), (ii)
         WHEN `a bookmaker licensed under this Act` THEN
             IF `b`'s `my age in years` LESS THAN `the age of majority`
             THEN `an offence by me`                                          -- s 22(1)(b)
             ELSE IF `b`'s `the bookmaker takes it as the Act allows`
                  THEN `lawful: the Act allows it`                            -- ss 5(1), 23(1)(d)(iii)
                  ELSE `an offence by me`                                     -- s 24(1)(c)
         WHEN `the wagering licensee` THEN
             IF `b`'s `it is a fixed odds bet`
             THEN `uncertain: ss 23(1) or 24(1)(b) read literally reach it, though the Act licenses or tolerates it elsewhere`
             ELSE `lawful: the Act allows it`                                 -- s 23(1)(d)(i): a totalisator authorised by written law
         WHEN `a friend or workmate, privately` THEN
             IF `b`'s `it is social gambling or permitted gaming under the Gaming and Wagering Commission Act 1987`
             THEN `lawful: the Act allows it`                                 -- s 23(1)(e)
             ELSE `an offence by me`                                          -- s 23(1)
         WHEN `an unlicensed bookmaker` THEN `an offence by me`                -- s 24(1)(b)
         OTHERWISE
             IF `Do I commit an offence under s 27A` `b`
             THEN `an offence by me`                                          -- s 27A(2), (2A)
             ELSE `uncertain: ss 23(1) or 24(1)(b) read literally reach it, though the Act licenses or tolerates it elsewhere`

-- The fine is the one the provision that names the case sets. For an `uncertain` bet it is the $100 000 of ss 23(1) and
-- 24(1) -- the most the literal reading exposes me to, not a finding that I am liable.
@export What is the most I can be fined for this bet, in dollars (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) ss 22, 23, 24, 27A)?
GIVEN `b` IS A `My bet` @desc Who you bet with, your age, where you are, the event, and how you bet
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for this bet` IS
    CONSIDER `What does the Act make of my bet` `b`
    WHEN `outside the Act: I am not in WA` THEN 0
    WHEN `lawful: the Act allows it` THEN 0
    WHEN `an offence by me` THEN
        CONSIDER `b`'s `who I bet with`
        WHEN `the TAB run by RWWA` THEN 2000                                  -- s 22(2)
        WHEN `a bookmaker licensed under this Act` THEN
            IF `b`'s `my age in years` LESS THAN `the age of majority` THEN 2000 ELSE 100000   -- s 22(1); s 24(1)(c)
        WHEN `a friend or workmate, privately` THEN 100000                    -- s 23(1)
        WHEN `an unlicensed bookmaker` THEN 100000                             -- s 24(1)(b)
        OTHERWISE 10000                                                        -- s 27A(2), (2A)
    WHEN `uncertain: ss 23(1) or 24(1)(b) read literally reach it, though the Act licenses or tolerates it elsewhere` THEN 100000

§§ `other offences that fall on the gambler`

-- Each is laid on "a person" or "no person", not on a bookmaker, RWWA or a licensee. Where no penalty is stated, s 30(1)(b):
-- "a penalty not exceeding $5 000".
DECLARE `Something I might do` IS ONE OF
    `place a bet for, or help someone bet with a bookmaker who is under a s 25 court order (s 23(2))`
    `place a bet or collect winnings for a person apparently under 18 (s 22A)`
    `as a person under 18, ask someone to place a bet or collect winnings for me (s 22(1)(c), (d), (2)(c), (d))`
    `as a person under 18, enter or stay in a TAB agency while it is taking bets (s 22(2)(a))`
    `take a person under 18 into a place where a totalisator is operating (s 21(2)(b))`
    `take liquor into a place where a totalisator is operating (s 21(2)(c))`
    `place a bet through RWWA for a person barred from places where a totalisator is operating (s 21(2)(d))`
    `keep a record of an interstate or offshore bet with an operator I know is not authorised (s 27A(3))`
    `not move on when police suspect I am loitering to bet (s 26)`
    `come back the same day after police removed me for unlawful betting (ss 26A(3), 26C(5))`
    `keep watch for police for unlawful betting (s 26B)`

@export What is the most I can be fined for this, in dollars (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) ss 21-27A, 30)?
GIVEN `what` IS A `Something I might do` @desc What you did
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for` IS
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `place a bet for, or help someone bet with a bookmaker who is under a s 25 court order (s 23(2))` THEN 20000
    WHEN `place a bet or collect winnings for a person apparently under 18 (s 22A)` THEN 10000
    WHEN `as a person under 18, ask someone to place a bet or collect winnings for me (s 22(1)(c), (d), (2)(c), (d))` THEN 2000
    WHEN `as a person under 18, enter or stay in a TAB agency while it is taking bets (s 22(2)(a))` THEN 2000
    WHEN `take a person under 18 into a place where a totalisator is operating (s 21(2)(b))` THEN 5000      -- s 30(1)(b)
    WHEN `take liquor into a place where a totalisator is operating (s 21(2)(c))` THEN 5000                  -- s 30(1)(b)
    WHEN `place a bet through RWWA for a person barred from places where a totalisator is operating (s 21(2)(d))` THEN 5000   -- s 30(1)(b)
    WHEN `keep a record of an interstate or offshore bet with an operator I know is not authorised (s 27A(3))` THEN 10000
    WHEN `not move on when police suspect I am loitering to bet (s 26)` THEN 2000
    WHEN `come back the same day after police removed me for unlawful betting (ss 26A(3), 26C(5))` THEN 10000
    WHEN `keep watch for police for unlawful betting (s 26B)` THEN 20000

-- s 28(2): "Where money is found in the possession of an offender convicted of betting, contrary to this Act, and is
-- proved to have been received in connection with that betting, the court shall order that the money be forfeited".
@export Must money I received from unlawful betting be forfeited (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 28(2))?
GIVEN `convicted of betting contrary to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of betting contrary to the Act
      `the money was found on me and proved to be from that betting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money was found in your possession and proved to have been received in connection with that betting
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my betting money be forfeited` IF
    `convicted of betting contrary to the Act` AND `the money was found on me and proved to be from that betting`

§§ `ss 10J, 21 -- what the operator may not do to me`

-- s 21(1): a bookmaker "shall not knowingly -- (a) bet with ... a person apparently under the age of 18 years; or (b) bet
-- with ... a person apparently under the influence of intoxicating liquor"; s 21(3)(a), (b) say the same of TAB staff.
-- The duty is the operator's; "apparently" is the operator's judgment, asked as a fact.
@export May a WA bookmaker or the TAB knowingly take my bet (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 21(1), (3))?
GIVEN `I appear to be under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you appear to be under 18
      `I appear to be drunk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you appear to be under the influence of liquor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a bookmaker or the TAB take my bet` IF
    (NOT `I appear to be under 18`) AND (NOT `I appear to be drunk`)

-- s 10J(2): "A wagering licensee must not accept a bet involving the provision of credit by the wagering licensee."
-- (s 29 does the same for RWWA by reference to s 63 of the RWWA Act, which is not deposited.)
@export May the wagering licensee give me credit for a bet (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 10J(2))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the wagering licensee give me credit` IS FALSE

§§ `s 25 -- an order that no bookmaker bet with me`

-- s 25(1): "Upon proof being given to the satisfaction of the Magistrates Court that any person by excessive betting is
-- likely to be impoverished to a degree where that person or any member of the family of that person is in want, the
-- Court may order that no bookmaker shall bet with such person for not exceeding the space of one year." (2): it may be
-- renewed; (3): RWWA, totalisator operators and bookmakers must give effect to it after notice; (5): it may be revoked.
-- The Act does not say who may ask the Court for the order. It lays no offence on the person named for betting.
@export Can the Magistrates Court order that no bookmaker bet with me (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 25(1))?
GIVEN `the Court is satisfied my betting is likely to leave me or my family in want` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Magistrates Court is satisfied that by excessive betting you are likely to be impoverished so that you or a member of your family is in want
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Court order that no bookmaker bet with me` IF
    `the Court is satisfied my betting is likely to leave me or my family in want`

@export For how many years at most can each s 25 order last (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 25(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many years at most can the order last` IS 1

@export Can the order on me be renewed (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 25(2))?
GIVEN `the Court thinks I have not reformed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is of the opinion that you have not reformed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the order on me be renewed` IF `the Court thinks I have not reformed`

@export Does the Act say who may ask the Court for a s 25 order (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 25)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act say who may apply for the order` IS FALSE

@export Do I commit an offence under the Act by betting while an order is on me (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 25(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence by betting while under the order` IS FALSE

§§ `s 32 -- a dispute with a racecourse bookmaker`

-- s 32(1): a dispute about a bet "made with a bookmaker on a racecourse ... shall be referred in the first instance to and
-- determined by the stewards", and a party may appeal to the Commission. (2): by notice in writing "(a) if the racecourse
-- is in the metropolitan region, within 3 days; or (b) in any other case, within 7 days, of that determination" (later
-- only at the Commission's discretion in special circumstances). (3): where only part is disputed, "payment shall be made
-- on the bet in so far as it is not so questioned or disputed."
@export Within how many days must I appeal the stewards' decision to the Commission (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 32(2))?
GIVEN `the racecourse is in the metropolitan region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the racecourse is in the metropolitan region (Planning and Development Act 2005 s 4)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I appeal` IS
    IF `the racecourse is in the metropolitan region` THEN 3 ELSE 7

@export How much of a part-disputed bet must the bookmaker pay me now (Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) s 32(3))?
GIVEN `the amount I say is payable` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you say the bookmaker owes on the bet
      `the amount in dispute` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of that amount the bookmaker disputes
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must the bookmaker pay me now` IS
    IF `the amount in dispute` GREATER THAN `the amount I say is payable` THEN 0
    ELSE `the amount I say is payable` MINUS `the amount in dispute`
